!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/meta-api.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/meta.tn"
@doc:"""
  A meta layer declaring two namespace types whose values stand as entries of a schema that imports it. `api` maps
  identifiers to `method` records, so `myapi => !api { get_orders => { ... } }` is an entry whose value is a map
  of methods, and `router` maps identifiers to `route` records, each naming the method it serves at a slot typed
  `meta.ref<method>`, reached through such an entry by a qualified name (`handler: myapi.get_orders`). A method's
  request, error and reply records are slots typed `meta.ref<record>` and its response any type, `meta.type_ref`. An entry
  built with either namespace type is a value, not a type; a processor that binds binds each value of the map to
  a host class of its own: the records `method` and `route`.
  """
!schema {
  status_name => meta.identifier
  method      => { request?: meta.ref<meta.record>  response?: meta.type_ref  errors?: [meta.ref<meta.record>]  replies?: {status_name => meta.ref<meta.record>} }
  api         => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.identifier  value_type: method }
  http_verb   => !enum [GET POST]
  route       => { verb: http_verb  path: text  handler: meta.ref<method> }
  router      => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.identifier  value_type: route }
}
